## Safety invariants — MIRROR, do not delete this section

<!-- Why a copy exists: path-scoped rules load LAZILY, and foreign scoping syntax fails
     SILENTLY — both measured on a production repo (HARNESS.md §3). An invariant that must
     never be violated cannot live only in a file that might not load. These bullets mirror
     constitution Articles I–III and VI. The constitution is the AUTHORITATIVE copy; amending
     it means re-syncing this block in the SAME commit (the mirror rule). -->

- **I — [DOMAIN INVARIANT]**: [the rule that IS the product. EXAMPLE: "business objects are
  registered in metadata and read at runtime — never hardcoded as structs."]
- **II — [SAFETY INVARIANT]**: [the rule whose violation is a breach, not a bug. EXAMPLE:
  "every transactional query filters `tenant_id` — no exceptions, admin included; dynamic
  queries are parameterized, never concatenated."]
- **III — [ARCHITECTURE SHAPE]**: [LAYER] → [LAYER] → [LAYER] → [LAYER]; [one-line forbidden
  coupling, EXAMPLE: "no queries in the transport layer"]. Detail:
  [`rules/architecture.md`](rules/architecture.md).
- **VI — Executable gates over claims**: "done" = the gate chain green — never a claim, mine
  included. Acceptance is proven by a **non-privileged third person**
  ([GATES §3](../gates/GATES.md)).

